      "dc_id": null,
      "dc_config": {},
      "cols_json": {},
      "parent_index": null,
      "last_updated": "2026-05-12T00:00:00.000000",
      "title_size": "h3",
      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Recipe lane",
      "order": 1,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "center",
      "body": "These two need a **catalog recipe**. ANCOM-BC writes one CSV per statistic per contrast, so `qiime2/ancombc.py` joins and melts them into the single long table the volcano reads; the taxon counts are melted out of the taxa barplot export with the taxonomy string split back into ranks. Set a contrast and a q-value cut-off on the left and the volcano narrows \u2014 the recipe is what makes those columns exist to filter on.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/catalog_conformance"
    },
